Restore Kueue's admission metadata on the pod templates of a running elastic job.

Kueue merges the PodSet label, the workload slice annotation and the flavor's
node selector and tolerations into an elastic job's pod templates once, when
the job starts, and the ElasticJobUngater finds Pods only by them. Re-applying
a running RayCluster's manifest replaces the atomic workerGroupSpecs list and
drops that metadata, so every later worker stays gated while the Workload holds
its quota. While the Workload is admitted, the job reconciler merges the
admitted PodSet info back into each template that lacks the PodSet label,
without changing replicas, and then deletes the job's gated Pods that lack it,
which never ran and are recreated from the restored templates.

